    "sourceText": "after CSSS26, §2, p. 143.",
    "sourceHtml": "after <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jalgebra.2026.04.058\">CSSS26</a>, §2, p. 143.",
    "leftHtml": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕜</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace=\"0\" rspace=\"0\">/</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></math> be a quadratic monomial algebra, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> generated by a set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> of paths of length <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>.</span> Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ℬ</mi></math> be the paths having no subpath in <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>;</span> their classes form a basis of <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>.</span> Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Γ</mi></math> be the paths all of whose length-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> subpaths lie in <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>.</span> Write <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></math> for the paths of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> in <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Γ</mi></math>;</span> in particular, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>Γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></math> and <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></math>.</span> For <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>⋯</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></math>,</span> membership in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Γ</mi></math> means <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></math> for <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></math>.</span></p>",
    "rightHtml": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝕜</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace=\"0\" rspace=\"0\">/</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></math> be a quadratic monomial algebra, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> generated by a set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> of paths of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> written in travel order. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ℬ</mi></math> be the paths having no subpath in <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>;</span> their classes form a basis of <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>.</span> Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Γ</mi></math> be the paths all of whose length-<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> subpaths lie in <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>.</span> Write <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></math> for the paths of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> in <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Γ</mi></math>;</span> in particular, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>Γ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></math> and <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>Γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></math>.</span> For <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>⋯</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></math>,</span> membership in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Γ</mi></math> means <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></math> for <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></math>.</span></p>",
    "applicationHtml": "The path basis is <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ℬ</mi></math>,</span> including the vertex idempotents. The smaller Bardzell complex uses <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Γ</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></math> in degree <span class=\"math-run\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>.</span>"
